        // So first part "note n1 already exists in vault ..." is printed without newline? Let's check: capture showed "note n1 already exists in vault src\x1b[0;31merror..."
        // So first part is printed, then error printed on same line? But we saw later with color, error is on same line? In our earlier raw, we saw:
        // b'note n1 already exists in vault src\x1b[0;31merror\x1b[0m: new location is same as old location\n'
        // So first message and error are concatenated without newline. That suggests original prints "note {} already exists in vault {}" using print! not println!, then error_print which prints with newline? Actually error_print uses println! which would add newline after error, but first message without newline would cause them to be on same line.
        // We need to mimic: print first part without newline, then error.
