                full_current.join(&name).with_extension("md")
            } else {
                full_current.join(&name)
            };
            if !source_path.exists() {
                // For note, need to check file, for folder dir
                if is_note {
                    error_print(&format!("note {} not found", name));
                } else {
                    // Could be note exists but not folder? Original gave folder not found if trying to move folder that is actually note? We saw earlier "folder n1 not found" when n1 was note. So check existence as folder.
                    // If source_path is file (note) but we are moving as folder, then it's not found as folder.
                    // Since source_path for folder case is dir, if not exist, it's not found.
                    // For note case, if folder exists with same name, but note file not exists, it should say note not found.
                    // So we already check source_path existence.
                    // But also need to distinguish if name is folder but we try to move as note? Then note file not found.
                    // For is_note true, source_path is file, if file doesn't exist, error note not found, even if folder with same name exists.
                    // For is_note false, source_path is dir, if dir doesn't exist, error folder not found.

                    // Additionally, for note case, if the path is directory, it should still say not found? Original gave note not found even though folder exists? Let's see earlier: we tried remove note f1 where f1 folder exists but note f1.md doesn't exist -> error note f1 not found. So correct.
                    error_print(&format!("folder {} not found", name));
